# =============================================================================
# VELO Backend -- the build context of backend/Dockerfile
# =============================================================================
# The backend is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT (context `.`,
# `-f backend/Dockerfile`). BuildKit reads THIS file, the one beside the
# Dockerfile, instead of a root .dockerignore -- which belongs to the frontend
# build and leaves backend/ out.
#
# An ALLOWLIST: everything is out, then exactly what backend/Dockerfile COPYs
# is back in. The root holds frontend/, .git, prototypes, load tests and
# documents; listing what to leave out would miss the next directory added.
# .env never enters the context: no line below names it, and the re-exclusions
# at the end catch one left inside an allowed directory.
# =============================================================================

*

!backend/requirements.txt
!backend/requirements-dev.txt
!backend/app/
!backend/scripts/
!backend/alembic.ini
!backend/logging.json
# BE-182: the edition table at the repository root, read by the runtime.
!editions.json
!backend/migrations/
!backend/tests/
!backend/pyproject.toml
# BE-192: the test stage needs them (tests/test_primer_env.py); no values.
!primer.yaml
!docker-compose.yml
# BE-193: the test stage needs it too (tests/test_primer_env.py, the root
# login of the storage stack).
!docker-compose.storage.yml
# BE-207: the test stage needs them too (tests/test_primer_env.py, the slot
# `texts` against the frontend that reads it).
!frontend/nginx.conf
!frontend/Dockerfile
!frontend/scripts/lib/texts-package.mjs
# BE-190 fix: the test stage needs them too (tests/test_primer_env.py).
!backend/ci.env
!.github/workflows/ci.yml
!.github/workflows/backend-tests.yml
!comms-profile/

# Inside the allowed directories: local leftovers, never part of a build.
**/.env
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.venv/
**/*.egg-info/
